{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>whose fat of their sacrifices, etc.</b> — this is the word of HaShem against their words, and the sequence of the verses follows this course: ״כִּי יָדִין״ etc., and He will take vengeance for what His servants suffered, and further because He will see that power is gone, etc., and He said, etc. — and HaShem retorted: ״אֲשֶׁר חֵלֶב״ etc. ״יָקוּמוּ״. And the matter is self-evident: the destruction of those who eat of their sacrifices — for they will not avail and will not save — and they will recognize that HaShem alone is the savior. And this is what He concluded saying: ״רְאוּ עַתָּה כִּי אֲנִי״ etc." "<b>Let them arise and help you, etc.</b> Since there are two types of idolaters: one who worships idolatry to a complete god, and one who worships idolatry to an intermediary — and concerning both of them HaShem commanded, as we explained in its place (Exodus 20:4). Therefore He said: concerning the one who worships idolatry to an intermediary, He said ״יָקוּמוּ וְיַעְזְרֻכֶם״ — mere help, for this reason they made it to assist, to be of benefit between them and the God of the universe. And concerning the one who worships idolatry to a complete god, He says ״יְהִי עֲלֵיכֶם סִתְרָה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ה׳ throughout is resolved as HaShem per voice rules for reverent abbreviations; each וגו׳ rendered 'etc.' marking his elided quotations.", 1 "The closing quotation יְהִי עֲלֵיכֶם סִתְרָה ('may it be a shelter for you') appears to allude to the immediately preceding verse (Deuteronomy 32:37) rather than the current verse; rendered as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:43.484708444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}